@startuml
title Relational Access - ConnectionHandle Ownership Lifecycle

hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype polyline
left to right direction

state CREATED
state "ACQUIRED\nOWNED" as OWNED
state "ACQUIRED\nBORROWED" as BORROWED
state RELEASE_REQUESTED
state PHYSICALLY_CLOSED
state LOGICALLY_RELEASED

[*] --> CREATED

CREATED --> OWNED : no active transaction\nDataSource.getConnection()
CREATED --> BORROWED : transaction-bound Connection exists\nreuse same physical Connection

OWNED --> RELEASE_REQUESTED : ConnectionHandle.close()
BORROWED --> RELEASE_REQUESTED : ConnectionHandle.close()

RELEASE_REQUESTED --> PHYSICALLY_CLOSED : ownership = OWNED
RELEASE_REQUESTED --> LOGICALLY_RELEASED : ownership = BORROWED

PHYSICALLY_CLOSED --> [*]
LOGICALLY_RELEASED --> [*]

note bottom of OWNED
Relational Access owns the physical Connection.
It is responsible for closing/releasing it to the pool.
end note

note bottom of BORROWED
The outer Transaction Component owns the Connection.
Relational Access MUST NOT physically close it.
Commit/Rollback/physical close happen at transaction end.
end note

@enduml
